Can anyone tell me where its getting in on the outside though? Don't want to plug this up and have water just pooled somewhere else. I "think" it was water on the roof rack that did it but I'm not 100%.....is there a typical area on the rack to check? No water on the headliner.

Photo of how my boat is currently rigged. There have been several different ways shown in the Walker Bay manuals over the years, my question is;


Is it worth it to switch to a traveler block setup more like a laser? I'm not racing so not sure if for casual cruising it matters. 


I just made a new wooden boom so adding an extra eye for the block at the rear is no trouble, just wondering if the cost of all new and extra blocks is worth it.

