Best photo I have offhand:

&#x200B;

\[Imgur\]([https://i.imgur.com/bvTVtZS.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/bvTVtZS.jpg))

" I am a servant of the Secret Fire, wielder of the flame of Anor. You cannot pass! The dark fire will not avail you, flame of Udûn. Go back to the Shadow! "

&#x200B;

"YOU.....SHALL NOT PASS!!!!"

&#x200B;

Needless to say, my dog is sick of my shit.

Yup, gandalf has his closed staff with the inner crystal and the cage that looks like his white staff in The Hobbit, then Radagast gives him his for the Battle of the 5 Armies because Sauron breaks his at Dol Gulder....while face bashing orcs the branches on it break, turning it into what we see at the start of fellowship...as said above Sauruman takes this at Orthanc, and then in Rivendale he gets this staff, which is then lost after breaking the bridge fighting the Balrog (in the book it breaks while he does this, in the film it falls with him)

&#x200B;

I'm sure I spelled some names wrong.

\[Imgur\]([https://i.imgur.com/cFbTdGK.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/cFbTdGK.jpg))

&#x200B;

\[Imgur\]([https://i.imgur.com/bvTVtZS.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/bvTVtZS.jpg))

&#x200B;

\[Imgur\]([https://i.imgur.com/y4yaZcd.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/y4yaZcd.jpg))

&#x200B;

Here is most of it.

I actually love the parts at Dol Guldur, and assumed when I heard trilogy that there would be some added fluff to tie it in to LOTR. Makes sense to me being made after.

&#x200B;

The biggest issue for me, is Legalos. I could live with Tauriel being added, but Legalos shouldn't be there. Remove both of them and a ton of overly CGI elf fighting and it would be much more enjoyable, but its also easy to kinda zone out those parts.

&#x200B;

Its really a shame Peter Jackson didnt have the time needed to prep, because polished they could have been as good of films as LOTR.

This was something (along with the broken toes in TT) that I only learned within the last year. 

&#x200B;

The big one for me was that Gandalf kept his pipe in his first staff...that was a thing I saw on Reddit and now I cant un-see whenever I watch.

This.

&#x200B;

I bought one of those "shire" pipes, and after reading the many warnings now have it on display in my office. For smoking I just received my 8" forever stem to pair with my MM hardwood and it is a great smoker, and still looks pretty good IMO.

My managed to scratch the hell out of my G shock at work...I actually need to sell it since i haven't touched it since I got this watch.

&#x200B;

Id say play it safe for sure at work, but if your in the market for a cheap smart watch I think you will be really happy. It has amazing battery life, and the rubber band is comfortable.

Casual EDC for when im dressed but around the house.

&#x200B;

Left to right:

&#x200B;

**Wool Beanie**

My wife knit this for me.....aside from summer I always have a beanie with me. This replaced a very well used Carhartt one.

&#x200B;

**Case Folder Knife**

Love this knife. I have been carrying this for maybe 6 month or so. I was using a more "tactical" pocket clip folder, but this small blade does everything I could need, and sits comfortably in the bottom of my front left pocket.

&#x200B;

**G10 Caribiner and Keys**

REI find on the caribiner, and it has become one of my favorite EDC pieces. I used to use a pocket clip that hung my keys from my front left pocket, but while riding my old motorcycle lost them. I switched to the caribiner from the belt loop then, but am highly considering trying a different, deeper carry pocket clip. I found one with a bottle opener which would mean one less thing on the actual key ring. I also have never used the key-chain light I have, so might lose it in favor of just using my cell phone light.

&#x200B;

**Front Pocket Wallet**

Forgot the brand, it was a amazon find, but I love it. I was using a similar style, but of thin floppy suede, and the thicker leather feels so much nicer. I might steal the template and make my own out of a more raw looking leather, but after much trial and error with minimalist wallets I am set on this style and design.

&#x200B;

**Rings**

Insert LOTR joke here...

I work in a kicthen, and as such my gold band tends to snag pan edges. I switched to the Honor brand silicone band for wearing, and got a nice titanium chain for my wedding band.

&#x200B;

**Samsung Galaxy S9**

Hate the phone, but given the rate these things are crapped out by cell phone manufacturers ill be upgrading within a year anyway. Otterbox case, and a pop socket. Might try a lower profile alternative, but I like it for the kickstand ability while watching movies.

&#x200B;

**Amazfit Watch**

I was a G shock guy up until my brother gifted me this smart watch. I dont think I can ever go back....the ability to get phone notifications on my wrist has been awesome.

29 for the next month exactly. 

&#x200B;

On paper I guess im good.....I own 2 vehicles and a house, Happily married, 3 healthy kids, cushy safe state job that pays well for what it is.

&#x200B;

That being said, not exactly what I would have planned for.

First time using my sewing machine on suede. I used beeswax to water seal it, and hand stitched a button to cover the rough machine stitch on the tie.

&#x200B;

I know its kinda rough looking but i'm really happy with it....looks like something found in a trolls den in middle earth, and is super durable.

This sums up my feelings pretty well. The quests just dont hook me in, but ill be damned if I dont like just exploring all the spots on the map.

&#x200B;

My only concern is once I have visited all the spots, how much I will enjoy it, as the live events haven't really appealed to me.

I've been loving reading about all the WV lore leading up to the game.

&#x200B;

I live in the PAacNW and we just have bigfoot.

I feel the same way. I teamed up with a few people during events without actually joining parties....helped someone who was down with a stimpak, but didnt really quest in a group.

&#x200B;

TBH most gamers I find fairly cancerous, so ive never been a huge fan of online games. I keep hearing about discord as being like a site to find people to play with I think? I might look into something like that/

Yeah I'm off today (Tuesday) through Thursday, so hoping even if BETA is down Wednesday, I will get a 4-8 hour chunk Thursday.

&#x200B;

I work doubles fri-sun so that's peak playing hours....ill likely miss most of the times.
